  "notes": [
   "The degree requires the core (14-15 units) plus one of three concentrations (CISCO, Linux, Windows). All blocks tagged option_group 'Concentration' belong to one of the three concentrations; the student completes every block of a single concentration (the CISCO option is the two CISCO blocks, Linux the two Linux blocks, Windows the two Windows blocks). Reviewer should check this grouping.",
   "CISCO concentration prints '[CISN 110 and CISN 111] or CISN 119' (3-4 units); recorded as a separate choose_units block with minimum 3, but the actual rule is either both CISN 110 and CISN 111, or CISN 119 alone. The concentration's printed total 17.5-18.5 is placed on the main CISCO block and includes this choice.",
   "Linux concentration printed units 17 and Windows concentration printed units 19 are recorded on the main block of each; these printed figures appear to exclude the 3-unit choose lists (totals 31-32 and 33-34 imply the concentration plus core).",
   "The catalog prints a separate Total Units for each concentration (CISCO 31.5-33.5, Linux 31-32, Windows 33-34) and no single total for the award, so total_units is left null.",
   "BUS 310 row prints '3 - 4' for the group (BUS 310 or ENGL C1000 or ENGL C1000H or ESLW 340); BUS 310 itself is printed as (3), so units recorded as 3 and the alternatives carry their own units.",
   "The degree statement says the degree is completed with the Local GE Pattern or Cal-GETC 'plus sufficient electives for a total of at least 60 units'; this is the standard ARC sentence, so degree_total left null and electives_fill_degree set true.",
   "The outcomes list includes concentration headings as bullets ('WINDOWS CONCENTRATION:', 'CISCO CONCENTRATION:', 'LINUX/UNIX CONCENTRATION:'); these are not outcomes and were omitted. Outcomes 1-3 are Windows, 4-8 Cisco, 9-10 Linux/Unix.",
   "Careers taken from the 'Career Information' section on page 431 that follows this degree's section."
